1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,270
The same color, but it looks different?

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:07,040
Square A or square B —
which one is darker?

3
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:09,210
A looks darker, obviously… right?

4
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:11,380
Let's connect them with a bar of one color

5
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:13,750
Huh? The bar and both squares
blend together!

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,350
Now let's erase everything around them

7
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,920
A and B are exactly the same color!

8
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:23,190
When there's a shadow, your brain figures
"it must really be lighter"

9
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:25,560
So it corrects B in the shadow
and sees it as a light square

10
00:00:25,610 --> 00:00:29,530
You don't see the light exactly as it enters your eye —
you see the color your brain works out

11
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:33,500
That's also why white paper in the shade
doesn't look gray to you!

12
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:35,750
That's the end of Secrets of the Eye, Part 2!

13
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,250
NEXT: Say the color of the words!
